.*.lock
.ledger.lock
.insights.lock
# The ledger's append lock at its FAIL-OPEN anchor (#348). The NORMAL lock sits in the git
# common dir (`<git-common-dir>/opencrabs-ledger.lock`), inside a directory no working-tree
# walk can reach; when git cannot be run at all (fork exhaustion, a git-less fixture)
# `tools/ledger.py` anchors the lock beside the ledger instead, and THAT file lands inside a
# declared directory -- so the tree declares its name.
opencrabs-ledger.lock
__pycache__/

# The derived ledger index: disposable, regenerable, ~2.9x the text.
.ledger-index.sqlite
